  "answer": "Create a basic FastAPI application and define your first path operation by following these steps:\n\n1. Import `FastAPI` and create an `app` instance.\n2. Write a path operation decorator using decorators like `@app.get(\"/\")`.\n3. Define a path operation function; for example, `def root(): ...`.\n4. Run the development server using the command `fastapi dev`.\n\nHere's an example code snippet that demonstrates this:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef read_root():\n    return {\"Hello\": \"World\"}\n```\nThis code creates a basic FastAPI application with a single path operation at the root URL (`\"/\"`) that returns a JSON response with the message \"Hello World\". [deployment/docker-7]",
